.TH PWD 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
pwd \- working directory name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pwd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Pwd
prints the pathname of the working (current) directory.
On maux this is the current ProDOS prefix, followed by a newline.
An unset prefix is printed as an empty line.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/PWD  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
sh(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 if the prefix cannot be read.
